  "about": "Where the Coach sends typed words when a plan is running, the server advertises plan_edit and nothing is open in the chat. planEdit = POST /health/programs/{id}/edits; program = the programme wizard's offer; dayPlan = the day-plan wizard; venue = the venue wizard; chat = POST /coach. The same bytes live in the monorepo (docs/fixtures/plan-edit-router-corpus.json), the iOS tests and the Android tests; each asserts its sha256 and passes every case. Merged from the iOS and Android drafts of 2026-10-23 (cases each platform authored; one case where the two apps' existing venue routing differs, \"what should I eat after a workout?\", is left out because it says nothing about plan changes). Version 2 (2026-10-24) adds the new-plan cases: \"make\" with \"workout\" is an edit only when no new plan is asked for.",
